@startuml 08b-briefing-cards
!include _style.iuml
left to right direction
title Briefing — the cards: the articles read, their passages, what is around them, and the analysis

package "Business" {
    class briefingService {
        + readStories()
        + importedCard()
        + anglesOf()
        + angleCardsOf()
        + cardAnalyses()
        + analysisArticles()
    }
    class entityService <<other feature>> {
        + briefingGroups()
    }
}
note top of briefingService
    Reads the chosen stories (08-briefing), 5 articles each, a trusted
    medium first, then the reader's language, one per medium; a story
    none of whose pages can be read, or whose card is on a refusal, gives
    its place to the reserve (2 rounds more at most). Step "angles": the
    angles, the official sources, the names and what the profile follows,
    together, none of them can fail the briefing. Then the analysis
end note
package "Reading the articles" as Reading {
    class googleNews {
        + decodeLinks()
        + isNotNews()
    }
    class crawlers {
        + Html()
        + Pages()
    }
    class readableCards {
        + readableCards()
    }
    class titles {
        + wholeTitle()
        + cleanTitle()
    }
    class readingOrder {
        + onceEach()
    }
}
note right of googleNews
    The real address of a news of Google
    News: 10 a briefing, 2 a story at most,
    only for the stories no feed lets read
end note
note right of crawlers
    Html: a plain fetch and Readability,
    Crawlee for the pages it missed;
    Pages, the fetch only, for a news
    added by its link (public addresses)
end note
package "Writing the cards" as Writing {
    class extract {
        + extractArticle()
        + passagesText()
        + translateTexts()
        + canSummarize()
        + sentencesOf()
    }
    class contested {
        + contestedOf()
    }
    class profileAi {
        + reviewCards()
    }
    class corroboration {
        + corroborationOf()
    }
    class hedging {
        + hedgedBy()
    }
}
note right of extract
    The AI gives the numbers of 5 sentences at
    most (170 words), shown word for word; the
    points (3) and the summary (65 words) are
    made of the same sentences. A translation,
    marked, its figures checked
end note
note right of contested
    A sentence of an article where
    someone named denies the news,
    found by its words, confirmed
    by one call of the AI
end note
package "AI version" as AiVersion {
    class aiWays {
        + aiWaysOf()
    }
}
note right of aiWays
    Points and a summary written by
    deepseek-v4-pro:0813, shown when the
    reader asks for them, marked; left out
    when a figure is not in the article
end note
package "Around the card (step angles)" as Around {
    class otherAngles {
        + otherAnglesOf()
        + nearCardsOf()
        + sameFactsOut()
        + placeAngles()
    }
    class affairNames {
        + storiesOfSameNames()
    }
    class officialSources {
        + officialSourcesOf()
    }
    class statements {
        + statementsOf()
    }
    class cardNames {
        + namesOfCards()
    }
    class wikidata {
        + searchItems()
        + readChannels()
        + exactItems()
    }
    class feedFinder <<other feature>> {
        + findFeeds()
    }
}
note right of otherAngles
    The stories of the last 3 days (or of the
    briefing's days) closest to the card (from
    0.6, 8 judged), and 5
    naming its rare names over 30 days; the
    AI judges them on their titles, 5 shown
end note
note right of officialSources
    The AI names the parties of the news,
    Wikidata their site and open accounts,
    their posts near the card are judged
    twice: 2 shown at most. With them, the
    statements its own articles report
end note
package "Analysis (after the briefing)" as Analysis {
    class cardAnalysis {
        + analysesOf()
        + pickedCards()
        + analysisOfCard()
        + checkedLines()
        + fittedArticles()
    }
    class tagger {
        + tagTexts()
    }
}
note right of cardAnalysis
    deepseek-v4-pro:0813 picks the cards that merit
    one (no reasoning), then writes, 3 cards at once
    and reasoning (300 s at most), why it matters and
    what may come next, each line citing its sources;
    the code drops a line whose figure or name its
    sources do not give. With the timeline of the
    earlier stories of the affair. Not awaited
end note
package "Data" as Data {
    class storyModel {
        + storyArticles()
        + closeStories()
        + likenessTo()
        + likenessAmong()
        + earlierInThreads()
    }
    class feedModel {
        + saveResolvedLinks()
        + searchArticles()
    }
    class officialModel {
        + names()
        + saveNames()
        + items()
        + saveChannels()
        + saveSiteFeed()
        + newsOfMedia()
    }
    class mentionModel {
        + namesOfArticles()
        + storiesNaming()
        + want()
        + setLink()
    }
    class briefingModel {
        + watched()
        + analysis()
    }
}
note right of officialModel
    party_names: the item of Wikidata
    of a name the AI gave; entities:
    the channels of each item
end note
class ollama {
    + ollamaJson()
}
class "News sites" as Web <<external>>
class "Ollama cloud\n(gemma4:31b, deepseek-v4-pro:0813)" as OllamaCloud <<external>>
class "Wikidata" as WikidataApi <<external>>
class "NER tagger (GLiNER)" as Ner <<external>>
class "PostgreSQL + pgvector" as PostgreSQL <<external>>


briefingService --> Reading
briefingService --> Writing
briefingService --> AiVersion
briefingService --> Around
briefingService --> Analysis
briefingService --> entityService : the news of what\nthe profile follows
briefingService --> Data
officialSources --> statements
officialSources --> wikidata
officialSources --> feedFinder : the feed of\na party's site
affairNames --> wikidata
cardAnalysis --> tagger
Around --> Data
Writing --> ollama
AiVersion --> ollama
Around --> ollama
Analysis --> ollama
crawlers --> Web
ollama --> OllamaCloud
wikidata --> WikidataApi
tagger --> Ner
Data --> PostgreSQL
@enduml
